367	// A "theap" is a thread-local heap. This API is only provided for special circumstances like runtimes
368	// that already have a thread-local context and can store the theap there for (slightly) faster allocations.
369	// This also allows to set a default theap for the current thread so that `malloc` etc. allocate from
